# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# The ssh host keys of this fleet, written by `meister-deploy keys enroll`.
#
# It is PUBLIC and it is committed: every ssh this tool runs uses
# `-o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes -o UserKnownHostsFile=<this file>`, so a
# host that is not in here is a host nothing talks to — and a host whose key
# changed is a refusal rather than a shrug (D10).
#
# `keys enroll <host> --fingerprint SHA256:…` takes the fingerprint from the
# installer output or the console, checks it against ssh-keyscan, and appends
# the key here. It never accepts a key it was not told to expect.
